                                                                ] ;
                                                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A bilaterally paired branched artery that originates from the aortic arches and divides into and includes as parts the internal and external carotid arteries[cjm]." ;
                                                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "we follow the FMA and treat the artery as a tree-structure - here we include the internal and external as parts. For the part that excludes the branches, see 'trunk of common carotid artery'" ;
                                                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000232> "This class represents the adult and developing structures'" ;
