###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001991
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001991> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001807> ;
                                                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "The cervical ganglia are paravertebral ganglia of the sympathetic nervous system. They consist of three paravertebral ganglia: superior cervical ganglion middle cervical ganglion inferior cervical ganglion. The inferior ganglion may be fused with the first thoracic ganglion to form a single structure, the stellate ganglion. Nerves emerging from cervical sympathetic ganglia contribute to the cardiac plexus, among other things. [WP,unvetted]." ;
